      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00054",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[54]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4843,
      "endIndex": 5015,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "1. Wash Cold: Always wash your work shirts and trousers in cold water. It protects the crispness of the collars and prevents dark colors (like navy and black) from fading.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00055",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[55]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5015,
      "endIndex": 5133,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "2. Inside Out: Turn your trousers and shirts inside out before washing to protect the fabric's surface from friction.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00056",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[56]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5133,
      "endIndex": 5271,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "3. Skip the Dryer: High heat destroys natural fibers and ruins the elastane stretch in your chinos. Air dry your clothes on good hangers.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00057",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[57]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5271,
      "endIndex": 5418,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "4. Ironing: A sharp office look requires a good iron. Iron your cotton shirts while they are still slightly damp for the crispest possible finish.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
